From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:26:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/26] Safarium: View > Always Show Toolbar in Full Screen

The menu item is back and works with Safarium's NSToolbar, like
Safari's: off, the toolbar slides down with the menu bar at the top of
the screen; on (the default, Chrome's pref kShowFullscreenToolbar), it
stays. ViewsNSWindowDelegate adds AutoHideToolbar in
-window:willUseFullScreenPresentationOptions: for windows that ask for
it (BrowserNativeWidgetWindow.autoHidesToolbarInFullScreen). AppKit only
reads this when entering full screen, so a change made while in full
screen applies the next time. The menu shows the pref's checkmark.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
